# Copy to .env (gitignored) and uncomment ONE provider block.
# Already-exported shell variables win over this file.
# Check what resolved:  python llm.py

# --- Web UI bind (optional)
# python server.py reads these. A shell export wins. Unset keeps
# 127.0.0.1 port 8000 (this computer only). Restart after changing.
# Use 0.0.0.0 to accept connections from other machines on the same
# network, then open http://<this-mac-lan-ip>:PORT
# (Wi-Fi address: ipconfig getifaddr en0, or en1 on some Macs).
# PORT must be an integer from 1 through 65535.
# HOST=127.0.0.1
# PORT=8000

# --- Website lock (required for python server.py)
# One shared password for Ask and Library. No usernames.
# The server exits if this is missing or empty. A shell export wins.
# CLI scripts do not read it. Do not commit a real password.
# LOCK_PASSWORD=replace-with-a-long-passphrase

# --- Corpus location (optional)
# Folder of markdown for chunking, Re-index, and the Library page.
# Relative paths are from this src/ directory, not the shell cwd.
# Unset keeps ./docs. Upload still writes a basename into this folder's
# root; nested *.md files are listed, indexed, and deletable. Restart
# the process and Re-index after changing. index/ stays next to these scripts.
# DOCS_DIR=docs
# DOCS_DIR=/absolute/path/to/markdown

# --- Anthropic (default if LLM_PROVIDER is unset and ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is set)
# LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic
# LLM_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# --- OpenAI
# LLM_PROVIDER=openai
# LLM_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# --- Ollama (local). Start the daemon and pull the model first:
#   ollama serve
#   ollama pull llama3.2
# LLM_PROVIDER=ollama
# LLM_MODEL=llama3.2
# LLM_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1

# --- xAI
# LLM_PROVIDER=xai
# LLM_MODEL=grok-4.5
# XAI_API_KEY=xai-...

# --- Any other OpenAI-compatible endpoint (Groq, OpenRouter, vLLM, LM Studio, …)
# LLM_PROVIDER=openai
# LLM_MODEL=your-model-id
# LLM_BASE_URL=https://api.example.com/v1
# LLM_API_KEY=...

# HF_TOKEN to enable higher rate limits and faster downloads
# HF_TOKEN=hf_**